/*
 * ============================================================================
 * Zamani Programming Language
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * File:
 *     grammar/interoperability/interoperability.g4
 *
 * Grammar:
 *     Interoperability
 *
 * Status:
 *     Production interoperability composition grammar.
 *
 * Language:
 *     Zamani
 *
 * Implementation baseline:
 *     Rust 1.97 / Rust 1.97.1
 *     Rust 2021
 *     unsafe Rust forbidden
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * PURPOSE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This file is the AUTHORITATIVE COMPOSITION BOUNDARY for source-level
 * interoperability in Zamani.
 *
 * It connects Zamani semantic programs with external languages, ABIs,
 * execution systems, hardware/software interfaces, quantum formats, HDL
 * formats, system interfaces, foreign functions, and future interoperability
 * mechanisms.
 *
 * This grammar describes INTEROPERABILITY INTENT.
 *
 * It does NOT implement:
 *
 *     - C
 *     - C++
 *     - Python
 *     - Rust
 *     - Verilog
 *     - OpenQASM
 *     - assembly languages
 *     - an ABI implementation
 *     - a linker
 *     - a loader
 *     - a runtime
 *     - a foreign compiler
 *     - hardware discovery
 *     - device discovery
 *     - network discovery
 *     - quantum compilation
 *     - quantum routing
 *     - quantum scheduling
 *     - QEC
 *     - ZQN
 *     - resilience
 *     - optimization
 *     - physical placement
 *
 * Those systems have separate owners.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * ARCHITECTURAL POSITION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 *     Zamani source
 *          |
 *          v
 *     canonical lexer
 *          |
 *          v
 *     parser grammar
 *          |
 *          v
 *     Interoperability
 *          |
 *          +--------------------+
 *          |                    |
 *          v                    v
 *       FFI/ABI             foreign-language
 *       contracts           integration contracts
 *          |                    |
 *          +---------+----------+
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *              semantic analysis
 *                    |
 *       +------------+-------------+
 *       |            |             |
 *       v            v             v
 *      types      effects      capabilities
 *       |            |             |
 *       +------------+-------------+
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *              canonical semantic IR
 *                    |
 *          +---------+----------+
 *          |         |          |
 *          v         v          v
 *     classical  quantum::ir  hardware/
 *        IR                    HDL/resource
 *          |         |          |
 *          +---------+----------+
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *              optimization
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *                routing
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *                scheduling
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *                 lowering
 *                    |
 *                    v
 *               ABI/runtime
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * OWNERSHIP
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * THIS FILE OWNS:
 *
 *     - interoperability declarations;
 *     - interoperability imports;
 *     - interoperability exports;
 *     - foreign-boundary references;
 *     - language identity at the semantic boundary;
 *     - source-format identity;
 *     - ABI/FFI composition;
 *     - semantic adapters;
 *     - type-boundary declarations;
 *     - value conversion declarations;
 *     - ownership-transfer intent;
 *     - lifetime-boundary intent;
 *     - calling-convention intent;
 *     - linkage intent;
 *     - compatibility constraints;
 *     - capability requirements;
 *     - effect requirements;
 *     - portability requirements;
 *     - foreign-resource requirements;
 *     - foreign-call intent;
 *     - foreign callable references;
 *     - foreign data references;
 *     - foreign type references;
 *     - callback-boundary intent;
 *     - asynchronous interoperability intent;
 *     - streaming interoperability intent;
 *     - cross-language semantic contracts;
 *     - target-independent interoperability metadata.
 *
 * THIS FILE DOES NOT OWN:
 *
 *     - lexical token definitions;
 *     - identifier syntax;
 *     - qualified-name syntax;
 *     - ordinary expression syntax;
 *     - ordinary type syntax;
 *     - function parameter syntax;
 *     - ordinary function declarations;
 *     - ABI implementation;
 *     - ABI layout computation;
 *     - linker behavior;
 *     - loader behavior;
 *     - dynamic library discovery;
 *     - filesystem access;
 *     - network access;
 *     - process creation;
 *     - symbol lookup;
 *     - machine discovery;
 *     - device selection;
 *     - physical addresses;
 *     - CPU register allocation;
 *     - GPU selection;
 *     - FPGA selection;
 *     - ASIC selection;
 *     - QPU selection;
 *     - physical qubit selection;
 *     - quantum topology;
 *     - scheduling;
 *     - routing;
 *     - calibration;
 *     - QEC;
 *     - ZQN;
 *     - resilience;
 *     - simulation;
 *     - optimization;
 *     - canonical IR.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * POCO-REAF
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Interoperability must preserve:
 *
 *     Program_Once_Compile_Once_Run_Everywhere_Anywhere_Forever
 *
 * Therefore this grammar MUST describe:
 *
 *     WHAT boundary is required
 *
 * rather than:
 *
 *     WHICH MACHINE IMPLEMENTS IT.
 *
 * For example:
 *
 *     requires capability::quantum
 *
 * is valid semantic intent.
 *
 * The grammar must NOT turn that into:
 *
 *     use device 7
 *     use qpu_127
 *     use 32 qubits
 *     use topology X
 *     use CPU Y
 *
 * Concrete realization is downstream.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * SCALABILITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * There are deliberately NO finite production limits on:
 *
 *     - interoperability declarations;
 *     - interfaces;
 *     - foreign functions;
 *     - parameters;
 *     - arguments;
 *     - adapters;
 *     - conversions;
 *     - capabilities;
 *     - effects;
 *     - language integrations;
 *     - source formats;
 *     - callbacks;
 *     - streams;
 *     - resources;
 *     - devices;
 *     - nodes;
 *     - cores;
 *     - threads;
 *     - qubits;
 *     - memory;
 *     - address spaces.
 *
 * Practical limits may exist in:
 *
 *     - parser implementation;
 *     - compiler policy;
 *     - available memory;
 *     - available storage;
 *     - operating-system limits;
 *     - runtime limits;
 *     - target capabilities.
 *
 * Those limits are NOT language grammar limits.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * SECURITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Parsing this grammar MUST NEVER:
 *
 *     - open a file;
 *     - access a network;
 *     - load a library;
 *     - execute foreign code;
 *     - resolve a symbol;
 *     - invoke a process;
 *     - inspect hardware;
 *     - allocate native resources;
 *     - dereference a physical address;
 *     - create a runtime handle.
 *
 * This grammar is declarative and inert.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * CANONICAL DEPENDENCIES
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * The composition root provides canonical versions of:
 *
 *     identifier
 *     qualifiedName
 *     expression
 *     typeExpr
 *     parameterList
 *     argumentList
 *     attribute
 *
 * These MUST NOT be duplicated here.
 *
 * Canonical ownership remains with:
 *
 *     grammar/core/names.g4
 *     grammar/core/attributes.g4
 *     grammar/types/
 *     grammar/expressions/
 *     grammar/functions/
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * SPECIALIZED INTEROPERABILITY GRAMMARS
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This composition grammar integrates with, but does not replace:
 *
 *     abi.g4
 *     ffi.g4
 *     foreign-functions.g4
 *     c.g4
 *     cpp.g4
 *     python.g4
 *     rust.g4
 *     openqasm.g4
 *     verilog.g4
 *     AssemblyLanguage.g4
 *     system-interfaces.g4
 *
 * Specialized grammars own their respective syntax.
 *
 * This file owns how their semantic contracts participate in Zamani.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * QUANTUM INTEGRATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * OpenQASM interoperability is a FORMAT/FOREIGN-LANGUAGE boundary.
 *
 * It must NOT create a second quantum IR.
 *
 *     Zamani/OpenQASM syntax
 *             |
 *             v
 *       OpenQASM frontend
 *             |
 *             v
 *       canonical quantum::ir
 *
 * The same rule applies to quantum interoperability through FFI or runtime
 * interfaces.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * HDL INTEGRATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Verilog/SystemVerilog/other HDL integration is a foreign-language boundary.
 *
 * HDL semantics are owned by the HDL subsystem.
 *
 * This file only declares:
 *
 *     - HDL interface identity;
 *     - import/export intent;
 *     - binding;
 *     - port/data contracts;
 *     - capability requirements;
 *     - compatibility metadata.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * DETERMINISM
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * No:
 *
 *     - semantic predicates;
 *     - actions;
 *     - random behavior;
 *     - filesystem access;
 *     - network access;
 *     - target-dependent parser decisions
 *
 * are permitted here.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */

parser grammar Interoperability;

options {
    tokenVocab = ZamaniLexer;
}

/*
 * ============================================================================
 * TOP-LEVEL INTEROPERABILITY ITEM
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This is the reusable composition entry point.
 *
 * The authoritative compilation-unit grammar decides where an interoperability
 * item is legal.
 */
interopItem
    : interopDeclaration
    | interopImportDeclaration
    | interopExportDeclaration
    | interopBindingDeclaration
    | interopCallStatement
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * INTEROPERABILITY DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Generic language-neutral interoperability contract.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 *     interop math using "C" {
 *         ...
 *     }
 *
 * The language/source identifier is semantic metadata.
 */
interopDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'interop'
      interopName
      interopLanguageClause?
      interopSourceClause?
      interopAbiClause?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * INTEROPERABILITY NAME
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopName
    : identifier
    | qualifiedName
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * LANGUAGE IDENTITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * The language is intentionally NOT an enum.
 *
 * This is essential for extensibility.
 *
 * Existing ecosystems can use:
 *
 *     C
 *     C++
 *     Python
 *     Rust
 *     OpenQASM
 *     Verilog
 *     SystemVerilog
 *     assembly
 *
 * while future languages do not require this grammar to change.
 */
interopLanguageClause
    : 'language'
      interopLanguage
    ;


interopLanguage
    : qualifiedName
    | stringLiteral
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * SOURCE FORMAT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * A source format identifies the representation being integrated.
 *
 * It is not a filesystem path and is not automatically opened.
 */
interopSourceClause
    : 'source'
      interopSource
    ;


interopSource
    : stringLiteral
    | qualifiedName
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ABI SELECTION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * ABI identity is symbolic.
 *
 * The actual ABI implementation belongs to abi.g4 and downstream lowering.
 */
interopAbiClause
    : 'abi'
      interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * BODY
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopBody
    : '{'
      interopMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopMember
    : interopInterfaceDeclaration
    | interopForeignDeclaration
    | interopTypeDeclaration
    | interopValueDeclaration
    | interopFunctionDeclaration
    | interopCallbackDeclaration
    | interopAdapterDeclaration
    | interopConversionDeclaration
    | interopCapabilityDeclaration
    | interopEffectDeclaration
    | interopRequirementDeclaration
    | interopCompatibilityDeclaration
    | interopLinkageDeclaration
    | interopResourceDeclaration
    | interopAttributeDeclaration
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * INTERFACE DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Defines a semantic boundary.
 */
interopInterfaceDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'interface'
      identifier
      interopGenericParameters?
      interopInterfaceBody
    ;


interopInterfaceBody
    : '{'
      interopInterfaceMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopInterfaceMember
    : interopFunctionDeclaration
    | interopCallbackDeclaration
    | interopTypeDeclaration
    | interopValueDeclaration
    | interopRequirementDeclaration
    | interopCapabilityDeclaration
    | interopEffectDeclaration
    | interopCompatibilityDeclaration
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * GENERIC PARAMETERS
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Genericity prevents interoperability contracts from encoding machine sizes.
 */
interopGenericParameters
    : '<'
      interopGenericParameter
      (',' interopGenericParameter)*
      '>'
    ;


interopGenericParameter
    : identifier
      (':' qualifiedName)?
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * References an externally-owned declaration.
 *
 * It does not import or execute the declaration.
 */
interopForeignDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'foreign'
      interopReference
      interopForeignBody?
      ';'?
    ;


interopForeignBody
    : '{'
      interopForeignMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopForeignMember
    : interopFunctionDeclaration
    | interopTypeDeclaration
    | interopValueDeclaration
    | interopCallbackDeclaration
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FUNCTION CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This deliberately resembles a callable signature without redefining the
 * repository's ordinary function grammar.
 */
interopFunctionDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'fn'
      identifier
      interopGenericParameters?
      '(' parameterList? ')'
      interopReturnClause?
      interopContractClause*
      ';'
    ;


interopReturnClause
    : '->'
      typeExpr
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * TYPE CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Foreign types are semantic boundary types.
 *
 * Layout remains downstream.
 */
interopTypeDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'type'
      identifier
      interopTypeBody?
      ';'?
    ;


interopTypeBody
    : ':'
      interopTypeSpec
    ;


interopTypeSpec
    : 'opaque'
    | typeExpr
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * VALUE / CONSTANT CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopValueDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'value'
      identifier
      ':'
      typeExpr
      interopValueInitializer?
      ';'
    ;


interopValueInitializer
    : '='
      expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * CALLBACK CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopCallbackDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'callback'
      identifier
      interopGenericParameters?
      '(' parameterList? ')'
      interopReturnClause?
      interopContractClause*
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ADAPTER
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * An adapter declares a semantic transformation between interfaces.
 *
 * It does not define implementation code.
 */
interopAdapterDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'adapter'
      identifier
      'from'
      interopReference
      'to'
      interopReference
      interopAdapterBody
    ;


interopAdapterBody
    : '{'
      interopAdapterMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopAdapterMember
    : interopConversionDeclaration
    | interopCapabilityDeclaration
    | interopEffectDeclaration
    | interopRequirementDeclaration
    | interopCompatibilityDeclaration
    | interopAttributeDeclaration
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * VALUE CONVERSION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Conversion is declarative.
 *
 * The compiler determines whether a safe implementation exists.
 */
interopConversionDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'convert'
      interopConversionSource
      'to'
      interopConversionTarget
      interopConversionContract*
      ';'
    ;


interopConversionSource
    : expression
    | typeExpr
    | interopReference
    ;


interopConversionTarget
    : typeExpr
    | interopReference
    ;


interopConversionContract
    : 'using'
      interopReference
    | 'with'
      expression
    | 'requires'
      expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * CAPABILITY DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Capability is semantic intent.
 *
 * It does NOT select a device.
 */
interopCapabilityDeclaration
    : 'requires'
      'capability'
      interopCapabilitySet
      ';'
    ;


interopCapabilitySet
    : interopCapability
      (',' interopCapability)*
    ;


interopCapability
    : qualifiedName
    | stringLiteral
    | '(' expression ')'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * EFFECT DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopEffectDeclaration
    : 'effects'
      '{'
      interopEffect*
      '}'
    ;


interopEffect
    : qualifiedName
    | stringLiteral
    | '(' expression ')'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * REQUIREMENT DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Requirements are deliberately separated from capabilities.
 *
 * Capability:
 *
 *     what the target can do.
 *
 * Requirement:
 *
 *     what the program needs.
 */
interopRequirementDeclaration
    : 'requires'
      '{'
      interopRequirement*
      '}'
    ;


interopRequirement
    : interopReference
      interopRequirementValue?
      ';'?
    ;


interopRequirementValue
    : '='
      expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * LINKAGE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Linkage identifies a semantic association.
 *
 * It does not perform linking.
 */
interopLinkageDeclaration
    : 'link'
      interopReference
      interopLinkageBody
    ;


interopLinkageBody
    : '{'
      interopLinkageMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopLinkageMember
    : 'name' '=' expression ';'
    | 'kind' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'abi' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * RESOURCE CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Resources are described symbolically.
 *
 * No physical resource count is encoded here.
 */
interopResourceDeclaration
    : 'resource'
      interopReference
      interopResourceBody
    ;


interopResourceBody
    : '{'
      interopResourceMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopResourceMember
    : 'requires' expression ';'
    | 'prefers' expression ';'
    | 'constrains' expression ';'
    | 'hints' expression ';'
    | 'capability' interopCapability ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * COMPATIBILITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Compatibility describes semantic compatibility requirements.
 */
interopCompatibilityDeclaration
    : 'compatible'
      'with'
      interopCompatibilityTarget
      interopCompatibilityBody?
      ';'?
    ;


interopCompatibilityTarget
    : interopReference
    | stringLiteral
    | expression
    ;


interopCompatibilityBody
    : '{'
      interopCompatibilityMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopCompatibilityMember
    : 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'feature' '=' expression ';'
    | 'capability' '=' expression ';'
    | 'constraint' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ATTRIBUTE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Interoperability-specific metadata.
 *
 * General attribute syntax remains owned by grammar/core/attributes.g4.
 */
interopAttributeDeclaration
    : 'attribute'
      identifier
      interopAttributeValue?
      ';'
    ;


interopAttributeValue
    : '='
      expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * CONTRACT CLAUSES
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopContractClause
    : interopOwnershipClause
    | interopLifetimeClause
    | interopNullabilityClause
    | interopRepresentationClause
    | interopCallingConventionClause
    | interopDirectionClause
    | interopAsyncClause
    | interopStreamingClause
    | interopBlockingClause
    | interopThrowsClause
    | interopRequirementClause
    | interopEffectClause
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * OWNERSHIP
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopOwnershipClause
    : 'ownership'
      '='
      interopOwnership
    ;


interopOwnership
    : 'borrow'
    | 'owned'
    | 'shared'
    | 'move'
    | 'copy'
    | 'in'
    | 'out'
    | 'inout'
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * LIFETIME
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopLifetimeClause
    : 'lifetime'
      '='
      interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * NULLABILITY
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopNullabilityClause
    : 'nullability'
      '='
      interopNullability
    ;


interopNullability
    : 'nullable'
    | 'nonnull'
    | 'unknown'
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * REPRESENTATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Representation is symbolic.
 *
 * It does not encode pointer width, register width, machine word size,
 * alignment constants, or other target-specific facts.
 */
interopRepresentationClause
    : 'representation'
      '='
      interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * CALLING CONVENTION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Calling conventions are symbolic semantic requirements.
 *
 * Concrete lowering belongs to ABI resolution.
 */
interopCallingConventionClause
    : 'calling'
      'convention'
      '='
      interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * DATA DIRECTION
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopDirectionClause
    : 'direction'
      '='
      interopDirection
    ;


interopDirection
    : 'in'
    | 'out'
    | 'inout'
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ASYNCHRONOUS INTEROPERABILITY
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopAsyncClause
    : 'async'
      interopAsyncSpec?
    ;


interopAsyncSpec
    : expression
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * STREAMING
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopStreamingClause
    : 'streaming'
      interopStreamingSpec?
    ;


interopStreamingSpec
    : expression
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * BLOCKING
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopBlockingClause
    : 'blocking'
      '='
      interopBlockingMode
    ;


interopBlockingMode
    : 'blocking'
    | 'nonblocking'
    | 'unknown'
    | interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ERROR BOUNDARY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Foreign failures must remain observable.
 */
interopThrowsClause
    : 'throws'
      interopErrorSet
    ;


interopErrorSet
    : interopReference
    | '{'
      interopReferenceList?
      '}'
    ;


interopReferenceList
    : interopReference
      (',' interopReference)*
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * EFFECT CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopEffectClause
    : 'with'
      'effects'
      '{'
      interopEffectList?
      '}'
    ;


interopEffectList
    : interopEffect
      (',' interopEffect)*
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * REQUIREMENT CLAUSE
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopRequirementClause
    : 'requires'
      interopRequirementExpression
    ;


interopRequirementExpression
    : expression
    | '{'
      interopRequirementList?
      '}'
    ;


interopRequirementList
    : interopRequirement
      (',' interopRequirement)*
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * IMPORT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Import establishes a source-level semantic relationship.
 *
 * It does not open a file or load a library.
 */
interopImportDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'import'
      interopReference
      interopImportSource?
      interopImportBody?
      ';'?
    ;


interopImportSource
    : 'from'
      interopSource
    ;


interopImportBody
    : '{'
      interopImportMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopImportMember
    : interopReference
      ('as' identifier)?
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * EXPORT
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopExportDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'export'
      interopExportTarget
      interopExportBody?
      ';'?
    ;


interopExportTarget
    : interopReference
    | '{'
      interopReferenceList?
      '}'
    ;


interopExportBody
    : 'to'
      interopReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * BINDING
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Binds a Zamani-visible semantic name to an external semantic entity.
 *
 * No symbol resolution occurs during parsing.
 */
interopBindingDeclaration
    : attribute*
      'bind'
      interopBindingName
      'to'
      interopBindingTarget
      interopBindingClause*
      ';'
    ;


interopBindingName
    : identifier
    | qualifiedName
    ;


interopBindingTarget
    : interopReference
    | stringLiteral
    ;


interopBindingClause
    : 'using' interopReference
    | 'abi' interopReference
    | 'language' interopLanguage
    | 'source' interopSource
    | 'requires' expression
    | 'with' expression
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * CALL
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Explicit interoperability calls.
 *
 * The parser does not invoke anything.
 */
interopCallStatement
    : 'interop'
      'call'
      interopCallTarget
      '(' argumentList? ')'
      interopCallClause*
      ';'
    ;


interopCallTarget
    : interopReference
    | stringLiteral
      '::'
      qualifiedName
    ;


interopCallClause
    : 'using' interopReference
    | 'abi' interopReference
    | 'language' interopLanguage
    | 'source' interopSource
    | 'requires' expression
    | 'with' expression
    | 'returns' typeExpr
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN REFERENCE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Symbolic reference to a foreign entity.
 */
interopReference
    : qualifiedName
    | identifier
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * LANGUAGE-SPECIFIC BOUNDARY DECLARATIONS
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * These rules intentionally identify ecosystems semantically rather than
 * embedding their complete grammars.
 *
 * The actual language grammar remains owned by its dedicated file/frontend.
 */


/*
 * C
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Canonical specialized grammar:
 *
 *     grammar/interoperability/c.g4
 */
cInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'C'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * C++
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * The spelling is accepted only as an interoperability language identity.
 * Actual C++ syntax remains owned by cpp.g4.
 */
cppInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'C++'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


interopNamedContract
    : identifier
    ;


/*
 * Python
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Python syntax remains owned by python.g4.
 */
pythonInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'Python'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * Rust
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Rust source syntax remains owned by rust.g4.
 */
rustInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'Rust'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * OpenQASM
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * OpenQASM parsing remains owned by openqasm.g4 and the quantum frontend.
 *
 * This grammar only describes the interoperability boundary.
 */
openQasmInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'OpenQASM'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * Verilog
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Verilog syntax remains owned by verilog.g4.
 */
verilogInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'Verilog'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * Assembly
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * Assembly syntax remains owned by AssemblyLanguage.g4.
 */
assemblyInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'language'
      'assembly'
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * GENERIC FOREIGN FORMAT DECLARATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This is the preferred long-term mechanism.
 *
 * New languages do not require a grammar change merely to become
 * interoperable with Zamani.
 */
foreignFormatDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'format'
      interopLanguage
      interopNamedContract?
      interopBody
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN TYPE REFERENCE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * References a type owned by another language or ABI.
 */
foreignTypeReference
    : 'foreign'
      'type'
      interopReference
      (':' interopReference)?
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN VALUE REFERENCE
 * ============================================================================
 */

foreignValueReference
    : 'foreign'
      'value'
      interopReference
      (':' typeExpr)?
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN FUNCTION REFERENCE
 * ============================================================================
 */

foreignFunctionReference
    : 'foreign'
      'fn'
      interopReference
      '(' parameterList? ')'
      interopReturnClause?
      interopContractClause*
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN CALLBACK REFERENCE
 * ============================================================================
 */

foreignCallbackReference
    : 'foreign'
      'callback'
      interopReference
      '(' parameterList? ')'
      interopReturnClause?
      interopContractClause*
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN SOURCE CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * A source can be:
 *
 *     C source
 *     C++ source
 *     Python module
 *     Rust crate/module
 *     OpenQASM source
 *     Verilog/SystemVerilog source
 *     assembly source
 *     another future language
 *
 * The grammar does not open or parse the source.
 */
foreignSourceDeclaration
    : 'foreign'
      'source'
      interopSource
      interopSourceMetadata?
      ';'
    ;


interopSourceMetadata
    : '{'
      interopSourceMetadataMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopSourceMetadataMember
    : 'language' '=' interopLanguage ';'
    | 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'abi' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FOREIGN MODULE
 * ============================================================================
 */

foreignModuleDeclaration
    : 'foreign'
      'module'
      interopReference
      foreignModuleBody
    ;


foreignModuleBody
    : '{'
      foreignModuleMember*
      '}'
    ;


foreignModuleMember
    : foreignTypeReference
    | foreignValueReference
    | foreignFunctionReference
    | foreignCallbackReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ABI / FFI COMPOSITION ADAPTERS
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * These wrappers deliberately delegate implementation to the specialized
 * grammars.
 *
 * The actual canonical definitions remain:
 *
 *     Abi
 *     Ffi
 *     ForeignFunctions
 *
 * The authoritative compilation root should import those grammars alongside
 * this composition grammar.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */


/*
 * ABI declaration adapter.
 *
 * This is intentionally a symbolic reference rather than a duplicated ABI
 * grammar. The actual ABI grammar remains authoritative.
 */
abiInteropReference
    : 'abi'
      interopReference
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * FFI boundary adapter.
 */
ffiInteropReference
    : 'ffi'
      interopReference
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * Foreign-function adapter.
 */
foreignFunctionInteropReference
    : 'foreign'
      'function'
      interopReference
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * QUANTUM INTEROPERABILITY CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Quantum interoperability is semantic interoperability.
 *
 * It may connect:
 *
 *     Zamani
 *       |
 *       +--> OpenQASM
 *       +--> quantum runtime
 *       +--> quantum accelerator
 *       +--> quantum simulator
 *       +--> foreign quantum library
 *
 * None of those forms creates a second quantum IR.
 */
quantumInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'quantum'
      quantumInteropTarget?
      quantumInteropBody
    ;


quantumInteropTarget
    : interopReference
    | interopLanguage
    | stringLiteral
    ;


quantumInteropBody
    : '{'
      quantumInteropMember*
      '}'
    ;


quantumInteropMember
    : 'source' '=' interopSource ';'
    | 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'operation' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'capability' '=' interopCapability ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * HDL INTEROPERABILITY CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * HDL syntax itself remains owned by the HDL grammars.
 */
hdlInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'hdl'
      hdlInteropTarget?
      hdlInteropBody
    ;


hdlInteropTarget
    : interopReference
    | interopLanguage
    | stringLiteral
    ;


hdlInteropBody
    : '{'
      hdlInteropMember*
      '}'
    ;


hdlInteropMember
    : 'source' '=' interopSource ';'
    | 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'module' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'port' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'capability' '=' interopCapability ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * HARDWARE/SYSTEM INTEROPERABILITY CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Hardware identities are symbolic.
 *
 * They are NOT physical addresses.
 */
systemInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'system'
      systemInteropTarget?
      systemInteropBody
    ;


systemInteropTarget
    : interopReference
    | interopLanguage
    | stringLiteral
    ;


systemInteropBody
    : '{'
      systemInteropMember*
      '}'
    ;


systemInteropMember
    : 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'resource' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'capability' '=' interopCapability ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'effect' '=' interopEffect ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * DISTRIBUTED INTEROPERABILITY CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This expresses distributed semantic boundaries without encoding a fixed
 * number of nodes or a particular topology.
 */
distributedInteropDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'distributed'
      interopReference?
      distributedInteropBody
    ;


distributedInteropBody
    : '{'
      distributedInteropMember*
      '}'
    ;


distributedInteropMember
    : 'interface' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'protocol' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'capability' '=' interopCapability ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'consistency' '=' expression ';'
    | 'reliability' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * RESOURCE-AGNOSTIC TARGET CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * A target describes an abstract execution requirement.
 *
 * It is not a machine declaration.
 */
interopTargetDeclaration
    : 'target'
      identifier
      interopTargetBody
    ;


interopTargetBody
    : '{'
      interopTargetMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopTargetMember
    : 'language' '=' interopLanguage ';'
    | 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'abi' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'capability' '=' interopCapability ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'prefers' '=' expression ';'
    | 'constraint' '=' expression ';'
    | 'hint' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FEATURE NEGOTIATION
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Feature negotiation is symbolic and capability based.
 *
 * It does not encode a finite target matrix.
 */
interopNegotiationDeclaration
    : 'negotiate'
      identifier
      interopNegotiationBody
    ;


interopNegotiationBody
    : '{'
      interopNegotiationMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopNegotiationMember
    : 'requires' expression ';'
    | 'prefers' expression ';'
    | 'fallback' interopReference ';'
    | 'alternative' interopReference ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * FALLBACK
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Fallback is semantic policy.
 *
 * The grammar does not select a machine.
 */
interopFallbackDeclaration
    : 'fallback'
      interopReference
      'when'
      expression
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * ADAPTIVE INTEROPERABILITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Runtime/compiler adaptation is expressed declaratively.
 */
interopAdaptationDeclaration
    : 'adapt'
      identifier
      'when'
      expression
      interopAdaptationBody
    ;


interopAdaptationBody
    : '{'
      interopAdaptationMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopAdaptationMember
    : 'use' interopReference ';'
    | 'fallback' interopReference ';'
    | 'requires' expression ';'
    | 'prefers' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * VERSIONED INTEROPERABILITY
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopVersionDeclaration
    : 'interop'
      'version'
      interopReference
      '='
      expression
      ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * REFERENCE / IDENTITY
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This is intentionally semantic rather than physical.
 */
interopIdentityDeclaration
    : 'identity'
      identifier
      '='
      interopIdentityValue
      ';'
    ;


interopIdentityValue
    : qualifiedName
    | stringLiteral
    | expression
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * COMPLIANCE CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 */

interopComplianceDeclaration
    : 'compliance'
      interopReference
      interopComplianceBody
    ;


interopComplianceBody
    : '{'
      interopComplianceMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopComplianceMember
    : 'requires' expression ';'
    | 'prohibits' expression ';'
    | 'supports' expression ';'
    | 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * SAFETY CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This is source-level policy only.
 *
 * The grammar cannot prove safety.
 *
 * Semantic analysis and Rust implementation must remain safe.
 */
interopSafetyDeclaration
    : 'safety'
      interopReference?
      interopSafetyBody
    ;


interopSafetyBody
    : '{'
      interopSafetyMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopSafetyMember
    : 'requires' expression ';'
    | 'forbids' expression ';'
    | 'allows' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * PROVENANCE CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Interoperability transformations must remain traceable.
 */
interopProvenanceDeclaration
    : 'provenance'
      interopReference?
      interopProvenanceBody
    ;


interopProvenanceBody
    : '{'
      interopProvenanceMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopProvenanceMember
    : 'source' '=' interopSource ';'
    | 'language' '=' interopLanguage ';'
    | 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * SERIALIZATION CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Serialization format is symbolic.
 *
 * It does not imply a particular machine representation.
 */
interopSerializationDeclaration
    : 'serialization'
      identifier
      interopSerializationBody
    ;


interopSerializationBody
    : '{'
      interopSerializationMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopSerializationMember
    : 'format' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'version' '=' expression ';'
    | 'schema' '=' interopReference ';'
    | 'requires' '=' expression ';'
    | 'attribute' identifier '=' expression ';'
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * INTEROPERABILITY CONTRACT GROUP
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * Allows multiple independent contracts to be grouped.
 */
interopContractGroup
    : 'interop'
      'contract'
      identifier?
      '{'
      interopContractMember*
      '}'
    ;


interopContractMember
    : interopCapabilityDeclaration
    | interopEffectDeclaration
    | interopRequirementDeclaration
    | interopCompatibilityDeclaration
    | interopResourceDeclaration
    | interopSafetyDeclaration
    | interopProvenanceDeclaration
    | interopSerializationDeclaration
    | interopVersionDeclaration
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * PUBLIC COMPOSITION RULE
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * The authoritative compiler/parser composition layer should use this rule
 * when it needs a single interoperability entry point.
 *
 * This rule intentionally includes only constructs owned by this composition
 * grammar.
 *
 * Specialized grammars remain independently parseable and are integrated
 * through semantic/format adapters.
 */
interoperability
    : interopItem
    | cInteropDeclaration
    | cppInteropDeclaration
    | pythonInteropDeclaration
    | rustInteropDeclaration
    | openQasmInteropDeclaration
    | verilogInteropDeclaration
    | assemblyInteropDeclaration
    | foreignFormatDeclaration
    | quantumInteropDeclaration
    | hdlInteropDeclaration
    | systemInteropDeclaration
    | distributedInteropDeclaration
    | interopTargetDeclaration
    | interopNegotiationDeclaration
    | interopFallbackDeclaration
    | interopAdaptationDeclaration
    | interopVersionDeclaration
    | interopIdentityDeclaration
    | interopComplianceDeclaration
    | interopSafetyDeclaration
    | interopProvenanceDeclaration
    | interopSerializationDeclaration
    | interopContractGroup
    | foreignTypeReference
    | foreignValueReference
    | foreignFunctionReference
    | foreignCallbackReference
    | foreignSourceDeclaration
    | foreignModuleDeclaration
    | abiInteropReference
    | ffiInteropReference
    | foreignFunctionInteropReference
    ;


/*
 * ============================================================================
 * INTEGRATION CONTRACT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * The final composed grammar must integrate this file approximately as:
 *
 *     source-unit
 *          |
 *          +--> declarations
 *          |
 *          +--> statements
 *          |
 *          +--> interoperability
 *                         |
 *                         +--> FFI
 *                         +--> ABI
 *                         +--> foreign functions
 *                         +--> C
 *                         +--> C++
 *                         +--> Python
 *                         +--> Rust
 *                         +--> OpenQASM
 *                         +--> Verilog
 *                         +--> assembly
 *                         +--> system interfaces
 *                         +--> future formats
 *
 * Specialized foreign grammars MUST NOT depend on:
 *
 *     quantum::ir
 *     hardware runtime
 *     scheduler
 *     optimizer
 *     QEC
 *     ZQN
 *     resilience
 *
 * The dependency direction remains:
 *
 *     syntax
 *       |
 *       v
 *     AST
 *       |
 *       v
 *     semantic analysis
 *       |
 *       +--> classical IR
 *       +--> quantum::ir
 *       +--> hardware/resource semantics
 *       |
 *       v
 *     lowering / optimization / routing / scheduling
 *       |
 *       v
 *     runtime/backend
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * HARD-CODING AUDIT
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This grammar contains NO:
 *
 *     MAX_DEVICES
 *     MAX_CORES
 *     MAX_THREADS
 *     MAX_QUBITS
 *     MAX_PARAMETERS
 *     MAX_ARGUMENTS
 *     MAX_NODES
 *     MAX_MEMORY
 *     MAX_REGISTER_COUNT
 *     MAX_REGISTER_WIDTH
 *     MAX_VECTOR_WIDTH
 *     MAX_GPU_COUNT
 *     MAX_FPGA_COUNT
 *     MAX_QPU_COUNT
 *     MAX_TOPOLOGY_SIZE
 *
 * Language names such as:
 *
 *     C
 *     C++
 *     Python
 *     Rust
 *     OpenQASM
 *     Verilog
 *     assembly
 *
 * are interoperability vocabulary, NOT machine limits.
 *
 * New languages can use:
 *
 *     foreignFormatDeclaration
 *
 * without modifying this grammar.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * NON-GOALS
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This grammar MUST NOT evolve into:
 *
 *     - a universal foreign-language parser;
 *     - a linker;
 *     - a loader;
 *     - a hardware description;
 *     - a quantum IR;
 *     - a classical IR;
 *     - a runtime;
 *     - a scheduling system;
 *     - a routing system;
 *     - a QEC system;
 *     - a noise model;
 *     - a resilience system.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * COMPLETION CRITERIA
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This file is complete when:
 *
 * [ ] ANTLR generates it without grammar errors.
 *
 * [ ] Canonical lexer tokens are used.
 *
 * [ ] Canonical identifier/name/type/expression rules are consumed rather
 *     than duplicated.
 *
 * [ ] No unsafe Rust actions or predicates exist.
 *
 * [ ] No filesystem/network/runtime actions exist.
 *
 * [ ] C/C++/Python/Rust/OpenQASM/Verilog/assembly are represented as semantic
 *     interoperability boundaries rather than duplicated language grammars.
 *
 * [ ] ABI/FFI remain delegated to their owning grammars.
 *
 * [ ] Quantum interoperability ultimately lowers through the canonical
 *     quantum::ir boundary.
 *
 * [ ] HDL interoperability remains separate from hardware realization.
 *
 * [ ] Capability, requirement, preference, hint, and constraint remain
 *     distinguishable.
 *
 * [ ] No machine size or topology is hard-coded.
 *
 * [ ] No fixed qubit/device/core/thread limits exist.
 *
 * [ ] Future languages can be introduced without changing the fundamental
 *     interoperability model.
 *
 * [ ] Positive, negative, scalability, determinism, and cross-domain tests
 *     exist in grammar/tests/interoperability/.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 */